# Superpowers scratch (progress ledger, briefs, review packages)
.superpowers/

# Go
/coyote
# The pre-rename binary name. Kept ignored so a stale build artifact left over from
# before the project was renamed cannot be committed by accident — dropping this
# line un-ignores a 22MB file sitting in the repo root.
/webrtc-chat
*.test
*.out

# Background scenes that are frames from copyrighted film/TV. They are untracked
# deliberately: the project's MIT licence cannot cover them (see
# THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md), and //go:embed all:assets would otherwise put them in
# every distributed binary. Kept on disk locally; the server discovers whichever
# images are actually present at build time (internal/server/scenes.go), so a clone
# simply gets fewer Scenes chips.
internal/web/assets/img/bg/*.webp
# Freely-licensed scenes are tracked; add an exception per file rather than
# inverting the rule, so an unlicensed image can never be committed by accident.
!internal/web/assets/img/bg/carina.webp
!internal/web/assets/img/bg/pillars.webp

# Soundboard clips are local-only by default, for the same reason as the scenes:
# most are cut from music or media the MIT licence cannot cover, and go:embed would
# put them in every binary. The server discovers whichever are present at build
# time (internal/server/soundboard.go). Add an exception per freely-licensed file.
internal/web/assets/sounds/board/*.mp3
!internal/web/assets/sounds/board/1f680.mp3

# Superpowers isolated worktrees (feature branches checked out under the repo root)
.worktrees/
